      "why": "The spec requires >=250 MSPS throughput, which forces a 1-result/cycle architecture (pipelined or pipelined_m). Pipelined is the canonical high-throughput CORDIC. To meet max_abs_err <= 2^-13, we need sufficient precision. For CORDIC, error is dominated by n_iter and data_width. Typically, n_iter ~ 12-14 and data_width ~ 16-18 give ~13-14 bits of accuracy. We focus on the region where LUTs are minimized while meeting the error constraint. data_width 14-20 covers the likely sweet spot; n_iter 10-16 covers the accuracy requirement; angle_guard and frac_guard are kept small to minimize area since the error budget is tight but not extremely so."
